# Claude Opus 5.5 — findings by GLM 4.7 Flash

- Source: Anthropic Claude Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`)
- Date: 2026-10-21 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Claude Opus 5.5
- **Short description:** Anthropic's flagship reasoning model (Sep 2026) optimized for long-running agentic coding and knowledge work at 1M context.
- **Provider / access:** Anthropic Claude API (`claude-opus-5-5`), Amazon Bedrock (`anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`), Google Cloud (`claude-opus-5-5`), Microsoft Foundry (`claude-opus-5-5`), Claude Platform on AWS (`claude-opus-5-5`); Chat Completions API.
- **Release / knowledge:** Released September 22, 2026; reliable knowledge cutoff Jun 2026.
- **IDs:** `claude-opus-5-5` (Anthropic API), `anthropic.claude-opus-5-5` (Bedrock), `claude-opus-5-5` (Google Cloud/Foundry)
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 total tokens (1M); 131,072 max output — verified via Anthropic docs.
- **Modalities:** Text in/out; reasoning (adaptive thinking, always on); tool calls (parallel, adaptive); JSON mode; adaptive effort (`medium` default). Supports thinking between tools and text between tool calls.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-21):** $4 / input MTok, $20 / output MTok per million tokens; batch API 50% off; prompt cache read 5% of base input price ($0.20/MTok), write 5m cache 5% ($0.20/MTok), 1h cache 8% ($0.32/MTok); prompt cache minimum 512 tokens.
- **Architecture:** proprietary closed weights; adaptive thinking (always on, cannot be disabled); no open weights release.

